{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"complex-sassy-blackfly","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\n`rebar-autodeploy` reports `\"up to date; no-op\"` while declared services are DEAD. On 2026-09-05 the\n`review-bot` and `opcert` containers exited at a host power cycle and stayed down for **24 minutes**\nacross at least twelve autodeploy runs, every one of which logged success.\n\n`LLM-Review` votes stopped landing for every session during that window. Nothing detected it; it was\nfound by hand while investigating why three changes sat at `Verified +1` with no LLM vote.\n\n## Observed\n\n```\ndocker ps -a\n  rebar-mcp-1d60c5f72ff0-8092   Up 20 minutes (healthy)\n  compose-gerrit-1              Up 22 minutes\n  compose-review-bot-1          Exited (127) 24 minutes ago     <-- DOWN\n  compose-opcert-1              Exited (127) 24 minutes ago     <-- DOWN\n\njournalctl -u rebar-autodeploy (runs every ~2 min, exit 0 each time)\n  {\"event\":\"autodeploy\",\"msg\":\"mcp reconcile: swept orphan mcp images (removed=0 kept-live+prev=1)\"}\n  {\"event\":\"autodeploy\",\"msg\":\"up to date (1d60c5f72ff008ddc3acdff42fd5b84ecdfb2752); no-op\"}\n```\n\nRecovery was a manual `docker start compose-review-bot-1 compose-opcert-1`; both came back\nimmediately and the bot resumed accepting webhooks (`POST /webhook 202`, `GET /health 200`).\n\n## The defect\n\nAutodeploy's liveness question is **\"is the deployed SHA current?\"**, not **\"are the declared\nservices running?\"**. Those diverge exactly when it matters. It also reconciles only the `mcp`\nimage — `review-bot` and `opcert` have no reconcile path at all, so nothing was even looking.\n\nThis is the session's recurring shape: a check that runs, reports success, and is silent about the\nproperty it exists to protect. Siblings: `erratic-sunny-genet` (Mirror Guard reports\n`healthy:false` when it could not reach the host), `deistic-conventual-blackmamba` (CI votes\n`Verified-1 FAILURE` on a cancelled run), `satirical-baryte-cat` (worktree GC hangs inside its own\nlock and every later run SKIPs).\n\n## Why it matters for stability specifically\n\nThe system's three services are Gerrit, the rebar MCP server, and the code-review bot. Two of the\nthree can be down indefinitely with the deploy mechanism reporting healthy. No alarm covers this:\nthe review bot has no liveness metric, so its absence is not a missing-data condition either — it\nis simply invisible.\n\n## Note on exit 127\n\nBoth containers exited **127**. The logs before death show the review bot failing to clone from the\nGerrit it SHARES A HOST WITH (`RPC failed; curl 28 Operation too slow. Less than 1000 bytes/sec`)\nand a tracker write timing out under lock contention. Whether 127 is an ungraceful-termination\nartifact of the power cycle or a genuine entrypoint fault is NOT established — worth determining,\nbecause those need different fixes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 Autodeploy detects a declared-but-not-running service and says so, distinctly from a\n      SHA-currency no-op.\n- [ ] AC2 It either restarts such a service or fails loudly. Decide and RECORD which; silently\n      restarting a container that is crash-looping is its own failure mode.\n- [ ] AC3 `review-bot` and `opcert` have a reconcile path, or a recorded reason they do not.\n- [ ] AC4 A liveness signal exists for the review bot such that its absence is detectable — today\n      it is invisible rather than merely unmeasured.\n- [ ] AC5 Both branches proven: a healthy deployment still no-ops quietly; a dead service is\n      reported.\n\n## Constraints\n\nNever use `--force` or any gate bypass. `timeout` does not exist on this macOS host (exit 127) —\nbound with `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV'`. Terraform apply is operator-authorized and must follow a\nreviewed plan. Do not touch the shared main checkout; do not `git stash`.","id":"5ee6-5523-2a12-46e0","parent_id":"0480-df66-b3df-4aee","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Autodeploy reports 'up to date' while review-bot and opcert are dead: 24min silent LLM-Review outage"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788654045640987001,"uuid":"34dda3c2-28d3-4c4f-9d85-d1ac137e9511"}